claimed: channel-ring — eliminate the root cause found by idiomatic-api-compare: Channel.State is an immutable value REBUILT per operation (new Queue + new case class + CAS of the whole thing), while zio.Queue is a mutable RingBuffer (verified in zio_3 sources: RingBuffer/RingBufferPow2, array slots + seq array + CAS'd positions, zero allocation per op). Three prior lanes swapped the structure INSIDE the rebuild model (Vector, Fifo) and all failed -- the rebuild itself is the cost, not the structure inside it. Plan: a lock-free bounded Vyukov MPMC ring (AtomicReferenceArray[A] + AtomicLongArray seq + AtomicLong head/tail -- generic, so NO casts; CAS loops, so NO thread blocking), built and measured STANDALONE first, wired into Channel only if it earns it. Bounded capacity only this lane; unbounded stays on the current path (filed).
